%% alt: Two caches in sequence. A request first checks an exact or semantic response cache; a hit returns a stored answer without calling the model. On a miss, the prompt is sent with its stable prefix first. On a hit, the provider's prefix cache reuses that prefix at a fraction of the input price. On a miss, it charges full price and any write fee. The model then produces the answer.
flowchart TB
  Q[Request]:::human --> E{Response cache<br/>exact or semantic}:::control
  E -->|hit| R[(Stored answer)]:::data
  E -->|miss| P[Prompt, stable<br/>prefix first]:::tool
  P --> PC{Provider<br/>prefix cache}:::control
  PC -->|hit: 0.1–0.5× price| M[Model]:::model
  PC -->|miss: full price| M
  M --> A[Answer]:::human
